<description>
Complete the foreground shape by mirroring it across the 2x2 marker square.

Input structure
- A dominant background, one source foreground color, and one marker color.
- The marker color appears exactly as a solid 2x2 square.
- Source pixels lie in one or more quadrants around that marker square.

Rule
- Use the center of the 2x2 marker square as both a horizontal and vertical
  mirror axis.
- For every source pixel, paint its vertical reflection, horizontal
  reflection, and 180-degree reflection in the same source color.

Key insight
- The green 2x2 square is not copied; it defines the mirror center for a
  four-way reflection closure of the red mask.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "source-color mask and the solid 2x2 marker square",
  "dst": "the missing mirror copies around the marker square",
  "transform": "reflect every source pixel across the horizontal and vertical center lines of the marker square, preserving the marker and all existing source pixels"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10-20 rows x 10-30 cols, background 0
  colors:
    source: 2 [observed], marker: 3 [observed]; exactly 2 non-bg colors
  marker:
    solid 2x2 square of marker color; exactly one such block in the grid
  source_shape:
    NxN bounding box where N = 3-5, containing 6-10 pixels (density 0.40-0.70)
    not a filled rectangle; need not be connected (1-2 components) [observed]
    not fully 4-fold symmetric [observed, to make the task non-trivial]
  layout:
    source occupies exactly the TL quadrant relative to marker (r < marker_top, c < marker_left)
    source bbox bottom-right corner is diagonally adjacent to marker top-left corner (gap = 0)
    no source pixel shares a row or column with the marker
  margins:
    grid large enough for the 4-fold reflected output; reflected extent = 2*N+2 rows and cols centered on marker
    all reflected pixels remain in bounds with >= 0 margin on every side
  transform:
    reflect every source pixel across marker center (horizontal, vertical, 180-degree)
    output has 4-fold symmetric source pattern; marker preserved unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. pick grid H (10-20), W (10-30), N (3-5)
    2. build the 4-fold symmetric output first
       a. design one NxN source shape in the TL quadrant (random sparse, density 0.40-0.70, not a solid rect)
       b. reflect it to all 4 quadrants to form the complete symmetric pattern
    3. place marker (2x2) so the TL source bbox bottom-right is diag-adjacent to marker top-left
       ensure reflected pattern fits within grid on all sides (>= 0 margin)
    4. derive input by erasing the 3 reflected copies, keeping only the original TL quadrant source pixels
